   Earth surface air (1.2 kg/m^3, g = 9.81)    : g/a0(rho) = 7.31e-03
   Earth crust (2700 kg/m^3, g = 9.81)         : g/a0(rho) = 1.54e-04
   solar photosphere (2e-4 kg/m^3, g = 274)    : g/a0(rho) = 1.58e+01
  [PASS] R5 the Earth's surface air is 'strong-a0' by the same classifier (ratio < 0.1, deeper than the BH* photosphere's 0.10)
         measured: 0.0073
         reading:  every laboratory torsion balance sits on the 'strong' side; the label has no dynamical content, so the layer coinciding with it predicts nothing the framework can be held to

